<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karelia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karelia is a region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a>, divided today between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Parts of it were held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the seventeenth century. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Peace of Nystad</a> in 1721 Sweden ceded part of Karelia to Russia, part of the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karelia.jpg" alt="Karelia" width="285" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Jniemenmaa · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Many_Karelias.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
